{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V3TxZy31Dc1TFZq8oXKksw","type":"tool_result","content":".ard:\n138\n142\n157\n158\n159\n160\n161\n165\n168\n174\n178\n184\n194\n203\n204\n205\n212\n213\n215\n216\n217\n221\n222\n223\n224\n227\n231\n236\n237\n238\n239\n241\n243\n247\n252\n254\n255\n267\n268\n276\n292\n297\n304\n305\n312\n40\n41\n42\n43\n44\n45\n47\n48\n49\n50\n51\n52\n56\n58\n59\n61\n89\nconfig.yaml\nreviewers\nscanners\ntriage\nworkers\n\n.ard/312:\ncosts\nlogs\ntriage-lead.md\n# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c6edd8e-925b-4e54-8b51-c52d408847af","uuid":"56f2b41b-2089-4e3d-9eca-e663c3c70dc5","timestamp":"2026-11-24T13:51:49.842Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".ard:\n138\n142\n157\n158\n159\n160\n161\n165\n168\n174\n178\n184\n194\n203\n204\n205\n212\n213\n215\n216\n217\n221\n222\n223\n224\n227\n231\n236\n237\n238\n239\n241\n243\n247\n252\n254\n255\n267\n268\n276\n292\n297\n304\n305\n312\n40\n41\n42\n43\n44\n45\n47\n48\n49\n50\n51\n52\n56\n58\n59\n61\n89\nconfig.yaml\nreviewers\nscanners\ntriage\nworkers\n\n.ard/312:\ncosts\nlogs\ntriage-lead.md\n# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autocl